# Veripsa release gate (auto-discovered). One gate per file -> two PRs adding gates add two
# FILES, never a shared line -> no false merge conflict on registration. register_gate is
# defined in run_gates.sh. Format: register_gate <test> <marker> <name> <ok_blurb> <desc> [tail]
# NOTE: NO backticks and NO dollar-sign in the desc/blurb text below (shell-eval fragility -- see CLAUDE.md).
register_gate "tests/test_refresh_title_and_cochange_count.py" "REFRESH-TITLE + CO-CHANGE-COUNT GATE: PASS" "refresh-path title determinism + co-change raw-count moat lock" "refresh-path check title is deterministic (the neighbor-refresh path posts the SAME rich per-verdict title the acting path renders -- never a degraded bare Veripsa) AND no customer-facing co-change string leaks a raw (N of M) co-occurrence count" "two output/UX P1s found by LIVE measurement of the real Veripsa checks on PRs 433-437, both root-fixed + locked here. (A) CHECK-TITLE NON-DETERMINISM: the neighbor-refresh path (a sibling PR open/sync/push re-renders an in-flight neighbor via _refresh_changes + _post_refreshes) used to HARD-CODE the check title to a bare Veripsa and discard render_pr_check's rich per-verdict title -- so the same PR's title silently DEGRADED from e.g. Veripsa -- Unknown to bare Veripsa whenever another PR last rendered it (measured: PR 435 showed bare Veripsa while identical-verdict 433/436/437 showed Veripsa -- Unknown). ROOT fix: thread the rendered title through the refresh payload (the summary already round-trips; the title now does too, plus a redacted fork title), and the pause-ack overlay branch takes overlay title exactly like the acting path. The gate proves the refresh path posts the SAME title as the acting path across clear/warn/serialize/unknown -- the straight non-overlay path AND the paused overlay branch -- and never a bare Veripsa (it is RED on the old hard-coded path, GREEN after). (B) RAW CO-CHANGE COUNT LEAK (moat rule raw counts banned, coverage percent OK): the co-change advisory line used to render the percent + lift PLUS a raw (co of n changes) graph co-occurrence count (the banned class -- it exposes the graph history depth/size, the moat). ROOT fix: DROP the parenthetical; the percent + the lift carry the whole signal. The gate proves NO customer surface (title/summary/comment, across verdicts + a fork PR + the degenerate-row mix) carries an N-of-M-changes count, while a positive check confirms the percent and the lift survive so the ban is precise, not a gut. PURE + offline (render + refresh + post + pause-ack are stateless over a main-impact dict; the gh and db are in-memory fakes), content-free, verdict + extractor unchanged" 26
